    body: `Few people ever handle a bare chip. They buy a board — and the board decides what a project feels like: how it is powered, which pins can be reached, whether there is a screen, a battery charger, a LoRa radio or a case. Hundreds of boards share the same dozen chips, so knowing the families saves hours of reading listings. This branch walks through them: Espressif's reference kits, the finished bricks of M5Stack, the thumb-sized XIAO and its cousins, the Feather, Thing Plus, Nano and D1 mini formats, boards built around a display, a camera or a long-range radio, and the smart plugs and lamps that turn out to have an ESP inside. The [board catalogue](#/tools/boards) lists them all with their quirks.`
