    body: `Sensors, displays, memory cards and other controllers all talk to the ESP over a few wires, by a handful of protocols that are forty years old and still everywhere. Three of them — UART, I2C and SPI — cover nine parts in ten; the page for each shows the bits on the wire (and [the signal lab](#/tools/signals) lets you send your own). Then come the buses of industry and vehicles, USB, wired Ethernet, and the audio and card interfaces.`
